Updating may not solve your problem in this case - simpleaffy only has the 
control probe information for some common-used chips stored in it's 
environment; it doesn't take them from the cdf. There have been quite a few 
posts about this on the Bioconductor list... so many that it would be 
useful to put some sort of caveat in the help files for affyQCReport and 
simpleaffy! At any rate, check out my previous post and the possible fix 
referenced in it:

